   "answer": "Based on the provided passages, multiple evaluation metrics are utilized depending on the specific study and benchmark:\n\n* **Latent Performance Profiling (LPP):** Uses intrinsic capacity metrics such as **minimum entropy**, **maximum intrinsic rank**, and **maximum participation ratio**, alongside extrinsic benchmarks like MMLU-PRO, BBH, and IFEval [2605.30018_0008].\n* **Post-Hoc Calibration Benchmarking (CalArena):** Evaluates performance using metrics such as **Brier score**, **Logloss**, **ECE\u221215** (Expected Calibration Error), **Kuiper**, and **Accuracy** [2605.30188_0044, 2605.30188_0041]. \n* **Vision-Language Understanding (PARCEL):** Uses raw scores and mean retention metrics across benchmarks like ChartQA, DocVQA, InfoVQA, SciCap, ST-VQA, TextCaps, TextVQA, and WidgetCap [2605.30126_0041].\n* **On-Policy Self-Distillation:** Measures performance improvement using final student performance metrics and the student-self-teacher gap [2605.30070_0004].",
